---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<DocsLayout title="Getting started" description="Install methodos and add typed procedural memory to an existing agent.">
  <div class="doc-shell">
    <div class="content-grid">
      <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page"><a href={`${base}docs/`}>← Docs home</a><a href="#install">Install</a><a href="#graph">Build a graph</a><a href="#adapter">Add the adapter</a><a href="#service">Run the service</a></nav>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">first 10 minutes</p>
        <h1>Start with<br /><span>one graph.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">Keep your solver. Methodos adds a typed, queryable memory layer around the actions your agent already understands.</p>
        <h2 id="install">Install the package</h2>
        <p>The core package uses SQLite by default. Install only the capabilities you need.</p>
        <pre><code>pip install methodos
# Optional capabilities
pip install "methodos[postgres]"  # horizontal deployments
pip install "methodos[vec]"       # sqlite-vec matching
pip install "methodos[eval]"      # evaluation harness</code></pre>
        <h2 id="graph">Build a graph</h2>
        <p>A graph describes actions, transitions, and the conditions that make a next step useful.</p>
        <pre><code is:raw>from methodos import Attribute, Edge, Node, ProceduralGraph, Relation

graph = ProceduralGraph(
    id="support-agent",
    nodes={
        "start": Node(id="start"),
        "search": Node(id="search", description="search a trusted source"),
        "answer": Node(id="answer"),
    },
    edges=[Edge(
        src="start",
        dst="search",
        relation=Relation.LEADS_TO,
        attribute=Attribute(
            condition="the answer needs evidence",
            guidance="search with a focused query",
            pitfalls="do not search with the whole conversation",
        ),
    )],
    terminal_ids={"answer"},
)</code></pre>
        <h2 id="adapter">Add the adapter</h2>
        <p>Implement the small async <code>Solver</code> protocol and inject an LLM client. The adapter owns the guidance context; your host owns observations and external tools.</p>
        <pre><code>from methodos import AgentState, PGAdapter, Solver

class MySolver:
    async def step(self, state: AgentState) -&gt; str:
        return "search"

adapter = PGAdapter(solver=MySolver(), graph=graph, llm=llm)
action = await adapter.step(query="Where is the order?", trajectory=[])</code></pre>
        <h2 id="service">Run the hosted service</h2>
        <p>For local development, use the CLI or Uvicorn. Production mode requires credentials and durable SQLite/Postgres persistence.</p>
        <pre><code>methodos init
uvicorn methodos.service:app --reload --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/health</code></pre>
        <div class="note">The default app is intentionally conservative: evolution work requires an injected durable runner. Do not run LLM evolution inline in an API process.</div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
